      "signpost": "against",
      "definition": "added to a noun or adjective to mean opposed to or against the thing named",
      "explanation": "Words made this way can describe people, groups, ideas, or actions: *an anti-war song*, *anti-smoking laws*. A hyphen is usual when the word is new or the next part starts with a capital letter (*anti-American*), and is needed when the next part starts with **i** (*anti-inflammatory*).",
